    "sections": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The Five Obstructions stands as Lars von Trier's fascinating meta-cinematic experiment with fellow Danish filmmaker Jørgen Leth. Von Trier challenges Leth to remake his 1967 short film <a href=\"/movie/1192527\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"1192527\">The Perfect Human</a> five times, each with maddening creative restrictions. The result is both a masterclass in filmmaking constraints and a psychological game between two directors. Like <a href=\"/movie/43003\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"43003\">F for Fake</a> (1973), Orson Welles' exploration of art and authenticity, it blurs the line between documentary and performance art."
      },
      {
        "type": "movies",
